                                "sense_id": "225479c4-96c3-3173-83c2-fc22c1c2e383",
                                "text": "1845, Hugh Miller, cited in Thomas Brown (ed.), Annals of the Disruption, Edinburgh: MacLaren & MacNiven, 1877, Part 2, p. 37,\nThe rude turf building we found full from end to end, and all asteam with a particularly wet congregation, some of whom […] had travelled in the soaking drizzle from the further extremities of the island."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "17ec33fb-0980-469b-a74e-ba7c8b7858ad",
                                "sense_id": "225479c4-96c3-3173-83c2-fc22c1c2e383",
                                "text": "1906, Oliver Onions, “Back o’ the Moon” in Back o’ the Moon and Other Stories, London: Hurst and Blackett, Chapter 17, p. 238,\nThe fire burned here and there for a fortnight, and then there came a light shower or two that set the hills a-steam with opaque white smoke."
